
Assignment title: Visual Prompt Studio Phase 1.1 
Prompt: Create a poster for a sci-fi movie where there is a crowd of people on the side walk and there are a cyborgs among them who have artificial limbs, or eyes. They are hiding in plain sight from normal people. The scene is of a the cross walk-in front of the Japanese Shibuya train station where one of the cyborgs is looking at the audience as if trying to make sure no one has noticed it is not human. The cyborg is wearing a hoodie that covers most of his body but shows his face. The other people are busy trying to get to work, some going to school. There should be a contrast in lighting focusing more on the cyborg looking towards the audience and the background being darker and creating a negative space in the distance. The camera angle should be of a higher angle and the cyborg should be facing the other way with just his head turned slightly to look at the audience. The clouds should be a bit dark with a ray of sunlight falling on the cyborg. The streetlights are portrayed by implied lines of the poles and slowing changing into implied lines that imply the lights instead. Nearby there are tall buildings that should have organic lines and slick, textile texture and have people working on their papers or using the computer inside.  And the name of the movie should be written in the middle part of the bottom “In Plain Sight”. 
Vocabulary breakdown:
Lines – Something that connects 2 points and gives an idea of the boundary of the object or idea of the shape of it.
Shape – Refers to the surface form of an object which is defined by lines and or color contrast.
Texture – Anything that lets us know or gives us an idea of what an object feels like to the touch.
Volume – The space that is occupied by an object.
Contrast – The noticeable difference between objects based on their colors, tones, lines, shapes, etc.

